  "reason": "Evidence: Multiprofile + scvi_n200 is the strongest configuration so far (0.653 acc), with aggregation choice (avgpool vs transformer) showing negligible difference (~0.3%). Image-only models are very weak (0.21), suggesting the RNA signal dominates. Uncertainty: We have not tested whether a pretrained RNA foundation model (scgpt) can outperform the variational encoder (scvi_n200) in the multiprofile setting. This experiment isolates the RNA encoder effect while holding profile setting (multiprofile) and aggregation (transformer, matching the best result) constant. Rationale: If scgpt substantially beats scvi_n200, it reshapes the entire multimodal strategy for the remaining 4 experiments by providing a stronger base for fusion. If it is comparable, we confirm scvi_n200 as the best RNA encoder and can pivot to testing multimodal fusion (e.g., scvi_n200 + ViT-L) in the remaining budget. This is a clean single-variable comparison that reduces uncertainty about the most important remaining design choice before committing to multimodal experiments."
